b.1--plan","local_name":"bob-cli-7b.1--plan","metadata":{"agent_clan":"bob-cli-7b","agent_clan_generation":"20261013081243","agent_session":"bob-cli-7b.1","agent_session_role":"plan","bead_id":"bob-cli-7b.1","changespec_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","cl_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-7b[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Capture links a dependency-blocked task by dropping its open [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]prerequisites[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Typing an existing-task link gesture (`@route:id`, `^route:id`, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`@route+id`, `@route+id!`, `@route:id=x…`) in `bob capture` or Bob [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]Mac Capture on a task that is Blocked only by its own open [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]prerequisites removes those prerequisites from its Depends-On line [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and then performs the gesture, while every case where dropping is [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]unsafe keeps today's consumption and says why.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]capture_link_drops_blocking_deps.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/capture_link_drops_blocking_deps.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-7b[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-7b/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Contract, dependency-drop writer, and the solo link gesture[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-core: write the §13.5 dependency-drop contract and PDG18–PDG27 [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]vectors first, then add the drop verdict, the staged drop writer, the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]shared guard helper, JSON/human output, and wire `@route:id` / [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`^route:id` (with `#name` and `=<X>`).[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Toggle, Ensure Next, and link-then-close adopt the drop[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-gestures[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-gestures: route `@route+id!`, `@route+id\\[#name]`, and `@route:id=x…`[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through the shared guard helper, print the drop line in their human [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]output, and convert their PDG1 tests into drop tests plus refused-drop [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]consumption tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bob Mac Capture presents dropped and refused prerequisites[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]mac[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac: decode `dropped_dependencies` and `link_guard`, add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dropped-dependency chip to the link, toggle, Ensure Next, and close [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]presentations, and (per mac_guard_detail) render bob's not-linked [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sentence; verify through macOS CI.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Decision record, supersession marks, and docs sweep[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]publish[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-gestures, mac[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]publish: sweep the docs for stale consumption wording and, under [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory_supersede, add the new decisions record, mark the two records it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]partly supersedes, and run `sase memory init`.[/#D7D7A